  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1802.37 Minor asbestos abatement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1802.37 “Minor asbestos abatement” means any asbestos abatement renovation activity which encompasses not more than 10 linear feet of RACM on pipes, 25 square feet of RACM on the surface of structures other than pipes, or 3 cubic feet of RACM on facility components where the length or area could not be measured that occurs within the context of a renovation or demolition. The term does not include larger projects that are divided into smaller segments.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-A 1800) #14104, eff 11-1-24, EXPIRES: 11-1-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html"
